1
00:05:44,444 --> 00:05:50,444
A legend will face his destiny.

2
00:11:28,888 --> 00:11:34,888
Indiana Jones and the Dial of Destiny is a adventure,
action film directed by James Mangold.

3
00:17:13,333 --> 00:17:19,333
Finding himself in a new era, and approaching retirement, Indy wrestles
with fitting into a world that seems to have outgrown him.

4
00:22:57,777 --> 00:23:03,777
But as the tentacles of an all-too-familiar evil return in the form of an old rival, Indy must don his hat and pick up
his whip once more to make sure an ancient and powerful artifact doesn't fall into the wrong hands.

5
00:28:42,222 --> 00:28:48,222
Indiana Jones, played by Harrison Ford.

6
00:34:26,666 --> 00:34:32,666
Helena, played by Phoebe Waller-Bridge.

7
00:40:11,111 --> 00:40:17,111
Dr. Voller, played by Mads Mikkelsen.

8
00:45:55,555 --> 00:46:01,555
Klaber, played by Boyd Holbrook.

9
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:46,000
Hauke, played by Olivier Richters.

10
00:57:24,444 --> 00:57:30,444
Teddy, played by Ethann Isidore.

11
01:03:08,888 --> 01:03:14,888
Indiana Jones and the Dial of Destiny is a 2023 American action-adventure film directed by James
Mangold and written by Mangold, David Koepp, Jez Butterworth and John-Henry Butterworth.

12
01:08:53,333 --> 01:08:59,333
It is the fifth and final in the Indiana Jones film series.

13
01:14:37,777 --> 01:14:43,777
Harrison Ford and John Rhys-Davies reprise their roles from the previous films, with Phoebe Waller-Bridge,
Antonio Banderas, Toby Jones, Boyd Holbrook, Ethann Isidore, and Mads Mikkelsen joining the cast.

14
01:20:22,222 --> 01:20:28,222
Set in 1969, the film follows Jones and his estranged goddaughter, Helena,
who are trying to locate a powerful artifact before Dr.

15
01:26:06,666 --> 01:26:12,666
Jürgen Voller, a Nazi-turned-NASA scientist, who plans to
use it to alter the outcome of World War II.

16
01:31:51,111 --> 01:31:57,111
Plans for a fifth Indiana Jones film date back to 1979, when a deal was made
with Paramount Pictures to produce five Indiana Jones films.

17
01:37:35,555 --> 01:37:41,555
Lucas began researching potential plot devices for a fifth film in
2008, and Koepp was hired to write the screenplay in 2016.

18
01:43:20,000 --> 01:43:26,000
In 2018, Jonathan Kasdan replaced Koepp but later left the project.

19
01:49:04,444 --> 01:49:10,444
Originally set for release in 2019, the film faced delays
due to rewrites and the COVID-19 pandemic.

20
01:54:48,888 --> 01:54:54,888
Steven Spielberg was initially set to direct but stepped
down in 2020, with Mangold taking over.

21
02:00:33,333 --> 02:00:39,333
Filming began in June 2021 in various locations including the United
Kingdom, Italy, and Morocco, wrapping in February 2022.

22
02:06:17,777 --> 02:06:23,777
Franchise composer John Williams returned to score the film, earning nominations for Best Original
Score at the 96th Academy Awards and Best Score at the 66th Annual Grammy Awards.

23
02:12:02,222 --> 02:12:08,222
Williams won the Grammy Award for Best Instrumental
Composition for "Helena's Theme".

24
02:17:46,666 --> 02:17:52,666
Indiana Jones and the Dial of Destiny premiered out of competition at the 76th Cannes Film Festival on May 18,
2023, and was released in the United States on June 30, by Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures.

25
02:23:31,111 --> 02:23:37,111
It grossed $384 million, becoming a box-office bomb due to
being one of the most expensive films ever made.

26
02:29:15,555 --> 02:29:21,555
The film explores themes of melancholy, treasure
hunt, ancient rome, sequel, flashback.
